<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73751" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμολογ-ουμένως</span></b> , Adv., c. dat.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>conformably with,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς εἰρημένοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					27
				</span></i>
			 : abs., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Oec.</u>
				1.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> in Stoic
			Philos., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. ζῆν,</span> with or without
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ φύσει,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Zeno Stoic.
				1.45
			</span></i>, Cleanth.ib.<i><span class="en">
				125
			</span></i>, Chrysipp. ib.<i><span class="en">
				3.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>by common consent, confessedly, admittedly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. μαχιμώτατοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					6.90
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.140
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				186b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hyp.
				<u>Lyc.</u>
				6
			</span></i>, etc. ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. ἀγαθοί, ὁ. ἄριστοι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>La.</u>
				186b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Mx.</u>
				243c
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ὁ. ἰητρική</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>VM</u>
					5
				</span></i>
			.</div>
